@startuml SplitSmartSecurityArchitecture
title SplitSmart Security Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Account holder" as user
component "Swing UI / future clients" as client
component "Authentication service" as auth
component "Authorization policy" as policy
component "Application services" as services
database "Encrypted credential store" as credentials
database "Expense and membership data" as data
component "Audit history" as audit
component "Receipt access control" as receipts

user --> client : credentials / session
client --> auth : authenticate
auth --> credentials : verify password hash
auth --> policy : account identity
client --> services : authenticated operation
services --> policy : group/resource check
policy --> data : membership and role lookup
services --> data : authorized transaction
services --> receipts : authorized receipt access
services --> audit : actor, action, time

note right of policy
  Organizer: membership and reviewer designation
  Designated reviewer: approve/reject expense
  Member: own/group access permitted by membership
  Non-member: deny without disclosure
end note

note bottom
  MVP uses local account/session handling; the full product must place authentication
  and authorization behind the shared service boundary. No password is stored in
  plaintext. Failed writes do not produce successful audit or balance changes.
end note
@enduml
